# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Paso 1: Mapear las entradas clásicas a un problema cuántico {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hamiltonian and reference state {#hamiltonian-and-reference-state}"
msgstr "Hamiltoniano y estado de referencia {#hamiltonian-and-reference-state}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This example uses a 12-qubit open-boundary Heisenberg chain ($n=12$),\n"
msgstr "Este ejemplo utiliza una cadena de Heisenberg de 12 Qubits con condiciones de frontera abiertas ($n=12$),\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H=\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\\left(X_iX_{i+1}+Y_iY_{i+1}+Z_iZ_{i+1}\\right),\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H=\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\\left(X_iX_{i+1}+Y_iY_{i+1}+Z_iZ_{i+1}\\right),\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with a single-excitation product state\n"
msgstr "con un estado producto de una sola excitación\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=|000001000000\\rangle\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=|000001000000\\rangle\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"as the reference state.\n"
"Because the Heisenberg Hamiltonian defined above conserves the total number of excitations, the reference state stays in the single-excitation subspace, whose dimension grows only linearly with the number of qubits. We can therefore compute the exact ground-state energy efficiently, by diagonalizing the Hamiltonian restricted to that subspace, and use it purely as a diagnostic benchmark for the KQD estimate. The KQD workflow itself estimates projected matrix elements by using Qiskit primitives and solves the resulting projected problem classically.\n"
msgstr ""
"como estado de referencia.\n"
"Dado que el Hamiltoniano de Heisenberg definido anteriormente conserva el número total de excitaciones, el estado de referencia permanece en el subespacio de una sola excitación, cuya dimensión crece solo linealmente con el número de Qubits. Por lo tanto, podemos calcular la energía exacta del estado fundamental de manera eficiente, diagonalizando el Hamiltoniano restringido a ese subespacio, y usarla puramente como una referencia de diagnóstico para la estimación de KQD. El flujo de trabajo de KQD en sí estima los elementos de matriz proyectados utilizando primitivas de Qiskit y resuelve el problema proyectado resultante de manera clásica.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set the parameters for the algorithm {#set-the-parameters-for-the-algorithm}"
msgstr "Establecer los parámetros del algoritmo {#set-the-parameters-for-the-algorithm}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Based on the upper-bounds on the Hamiltonian norm, Ref. [\\[1\\]](#references) heuristically suggests the time step $\\Delta t$ as $\\pi/\\|H\\|$.\n"
"Because the spectral norm $\\|H\\|$ is hard to compute, we instead use its upper bound:\n"
msgstr ""
"Basándose en las cotas superiores de la norma del Hamiltoniano, la Ref. [\\[1\\]](#references) sugiere heurísticamente el paso de tiempo $\\Delta t$ como $\\pi/\\|H\\|$.\n"
"Dado que la norma espectral $\\|H\\|$ es difícil de calcular, utilizamos en su lugar su cota superior:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\|H\\| \\le \\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\\underbrace{\\|X_i X_{i+1}+Y_{i} Y_{i+1}+Z_{i} Z_{i+1}\\|}_{4 \\times 4 \\text{ matrix, easy to calculate the norm}} = 3(n-1).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\|H\\| \\le \\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\\underbrace{\\|X_i X_{i+1}+Y_{i} Y_{i+1}+Z_{i} Z_{i+1}\\|}_{4 \\times 4 \\text{ matrix, easy to calculate the norm}} = 3(n-1).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We set the Krylov dimension to $r=10$ and the number of Trotter steps per time step to $5$: a large enough Krylov space to resolve the low-lying spectrum while keeping the deepest circuit ($t_{\\max}=(r-1)\\Delta t$) affordable, and enough Trotter steps to keep the discretization error small at that deepest circuit.\n"
msgstr "Establecemos la dimensión de Krylov en $r=10$ y el número de pasos de Trotter por paso de tiempo en $5$: un espacio de Krylov lo suficientemente grande como para resolver el espectro de baja energía manteniendo asequible el circuito más profundo ($t_{\\max}=(r-1)\\Delta t$), y suficientes pasos de Trotter para mantener pequeño el error de discretización en ese circuito más profundo.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build circuit {#build-circuit}"
msgstr "Construir circuito {#build-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, we build the circuits to estimate the matrix elements $\\mathcal{H}_{k\\ell}$ and $\\mathcal{S}_{k\\ell}$.\n"
"Because all powers of $H$ commute, we have\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}_{k\\ell}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Aquí, construimos los circuitos para estimar los elementos de matriz $\\mathcal{H}_{k\\ell}$ y $\\mathcal{S}_{k\\ell}$.\n"
"Dado que todas las potencias de $H$ conmutan, tenemos\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}_{k\\ell}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\langle\\psi_{0}|H e^{-i(\\ell-k)\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\mathcal{H}_{0,\\ell-k},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{S}_{k\\ell}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"\\langle\\psi_{0}|H e^{-i(\\ell-k)\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\mathcal{H}_{0,\\ell-k},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{S}_{k\\ell}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\langle\\psi_{0}|e^{-i(\\ell-k)\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\mathcal{S}_{0,\\ell-k}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"Such matrices where the elements depend on the index differences in this manner are called *Toeplitz* and can be reconstructed from first-row elements indexed by $d=\\ell-k$.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\langle\\psi_{0}|e^{-i(\\ell-k)\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\mathcal{S}_{0,\\ell-k}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"Such matrices where the elements depend on the index differences in this manner are called *Toeplitz* and can be reconstructed from first-row elements indexed by $d=\\ell-k$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, we present the circuit, called **extended-swap-test**, which prepares\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle=\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle+|1\\rangle|\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"where $|\\psi_d\\rangle=e^{-id\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Aquí, presentamos el circuito, llamado **prueba de intercambio extendida**, que prepara\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle=\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle+|1\\rangle|\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"donde $|\\psi_d\\rangle=e^{-id\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reference state {#reference-state}"
msgstr "Estado de referencia {#reference-state}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We prepare the reference state $|\\psi_0\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Preparamos el estado de referencia $|\\psi_0\\rangle$.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/fb2879c5-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/fb2879c5-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Time evolution {#time-evolution}"
msgstr "Evolución temporal {#time-evolution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Realize the time-evolution operator generated by the Hamiltonian, approximated by simple [Lie-Trotterization](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter).\n"
msgstr "Implementa el operador de evolución temporal generado por el Hamiltoniano, aproximado mediante una simple [Lie-Trotterización](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter).\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/017b8548-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/017b8548-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Extended swap test circuit [\\[3\\]](#references) {#extended-swap-test-circuit-3references}"
msgstr "Circuito de prueba de intercambio extendida [\\[3\\]](#references) {#extended-swap-test-circuit-3references}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit first prepares the reference state on the system register while the ancilla remains in $|0\\rangle$:\n"
msgstr "El circuito primero prepara el estado de referencia en el registro del sistema mientras el ancilla permanece en $|0\\rangle$:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"|0\\rangle |\\psi_{0}\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"|0\\rangle |\\psi_{0}\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then, applying a Hadamard gate to the ancilla creates a coherent superposition of two branches:\n"
msgstr "Luego, al aplicar una puerta Hadamard al ancilla se crea una superposición coherente de dos ramas:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, the controlled time-evolution gate applies:\n"
msgstr "Finalmente, se aplica la puerta de evolución temporal controlada:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"U(t=d\\Delta t) = e^{-id\\Delta t H}\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"U(t=d\\Delta t) = e^{-id\\Delta t H}\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "only when the ancilla is in the $|1\\rangle$ branch. Therefore,\n"
msgstr "solo cuando el ancilla está en la rama $|1\\rangle$. Por lo tanto,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(d\\Delta t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(d\\Delta t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the next code block, we implement:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Psi(t)\\rangle = \\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"which will be assigned as $t=d\\Delta t$ for $d=1,\\cdots r-1$ in the execution step.\n"
msgstr ""
"En el siguiente bloque de código, implementamos:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Psi(t)\\rangle = \\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"que se asignará como $t=d\\Delta t$ para $d=1,\\cdots r-1$ en el paso de ejecución.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/1260f66a-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/1260f66a-0.avif)\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Observables {#observables}"
msgstr "Observables {#observables}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For any Hermitian system observable $O$, here we set the observables to calculate:\n"
msgstr "Para cualquier observable hermítico del sistema $O$, aquí establecemos los observables a calcular:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"z=\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"z=\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is because $O=I$ gives the overlap element $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}=\\langle\\psi_0|\\psi_d\\rangle$, while $O=H$ gives the Hamiltonian element $\\mathcal{H}_{0d}=\\langle\\psi_0|H|\\psi_d\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Esto es porque $O=I$ da el elemento de solapamiento $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}=\\langle\\psi_0|\\psi_d\\rangle$, mientras que $O=H$ da el elemento del Hamiltoniano $\\mathcal{H}_{0d}=\\langle\\psi_0|H|\\psi_d\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using $X=|0\\rangle\\langle 1|+|1\\rangle\\langle 0|$, we have\n"
msgstr "Usando $X=|0\\rangle\\langle 1|+|1\\rangle\\langle 0|$, tenemos\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\langle \\Psi_{0d}|X\\otimes O| \\Psi_{0d} \\rangle\n"
"&=\n"
"\\left(\\frac{\\langle0|\\langle\\psi_0| + \\langle1| \\langle\\psi_d|}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)(X\\otimes O)\\left(\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\langle \\psi_d|O|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{z+z^*}{2}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\langle \\Psi_{0d}|X\\otimes O| \\Psi_{0d} \\rangle\n"
"&=\n"
"\\left(\\frac{\\langle0|\\langle\\psi_0| + \\langle1| \\langle\\psi_d|}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)(X\\otimes O)\\left(\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\langle \\psi_d|O|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{z+z^*}{2}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\operatorname{Re} z.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\operatorname{Re} z.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Similarly, using $Y=-i|0\\rangle\\langle 1|+i|1\\rangle\\langle 0|$,\n"
msgstr "De manera similar, usando $Y=-i|0\\rangle\\langle 1|+i|1\\rangle\\langle 0|$,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\langle \\Psi_{0d}|Y\\otimes O| \\Psi_{0d} \\rangle\n"
"&=\n"
"\\left(\\frac{\\langle0|\\langle\\psi_0| + \\langle1| \\langle\\psi_d|}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)(Y\\otimes O)\\left(\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"-i\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"i\\langle \\psi_d|O|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{-iz+iz^*}{2}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\langle \\Psi_{0d}|Y\\otimes O| \\Psi_{0d} \\rangle\n"
"&=\n"
"\\left(\\frac{\\langle0|\\langle\\psi_0| + \\langle1| \\langle\\psi_d|}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)(Y\\otimes O)\\left(\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"-i\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"i\\langle \\psi_d|O|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{-iz+iz^*}{2}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\operatorname{Im} z.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\operatorname{Im} z.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Therefore, we have\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\langle \\Phi_{0d}|X\\otimes O|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Por lo tanto, tenemos\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\langle \\Phi_{0d}|X\\otimes O|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\operatorname{Re}\\langle\\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle ,\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\langle \\Phi_{0d}|Y\\otimes O|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"\\operatorname{Re}\\langle\\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle ,\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\langle \\Phi_{0d}|Y\\otimes O|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\operatorname{Im}\\langle\\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\operatorname{Im}\\langle\\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, for each state $|\\Psi_{0d}\\rangle$, we need to measure:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"X \\otimes I \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Re}\\mathcal{S}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"Y \\otimes I \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Im}\\mathcal{S}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"X \\otimes H \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Re}\\mathcal{H}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"Y \\otimes H \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Im}\\mathcal{H}_{0d}.\\\\\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Finalmente, para cada estado $|\\Psi_{0d}\\rangle$, necesitamos medir:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"X \\otimes I \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Re}\\mathcal{S}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"Y \\otimes I \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Im}\\mathcal{S}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"X \\otimes H \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Re}\\mathcal{H}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"Y \\otimes H \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Im}\\mathcal{H}_{0d}.\\\\\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the estimation of the $\\mathcal{H}$ matrix elements, the number of Pauli terms is much larger than that for the $\\mathcal{S}$ matrix elements.\n"
msgstr "Para la estimación de los elementos de matriz de $\\mathcal{H}$, el número de términos de Pauli es mucho mayor que para los elementos de matriz de $\\mathcal{S}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can now reduce the number of measured Hamiltonian terms by using a shifting technique [\\[4\\]](#references).\n"
"We split the Hamiltonian as:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ahora podemos reducir el número de términos del Hamiltoniano medidos utilizando una técnica de desplazamiento [\\[4\\]](#references).\n"
"Dividimos el Hamiltoniano como:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H = (H-T) + T,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H = (H-T) + T,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $T$ is chosen such that the reference state is its eigenstate,\n"
msgstr "donde $T$ se elige de manera que el estado de referencia sea su autoestado,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T|\\psi_0\\rangle = \\tau |\\psi_0\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T|\\psi_0\\rangle = \\tau |\\psi_0\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then,\n"
msgstr "Then,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}_{0d}\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|H|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|T|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\langle\\psi_0|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}_{0d}\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|H|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|T|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\langle\\psi_0|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here,\n"
msgstr "Here,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is the shifted Hamiltonian matrix element.\n"
"Therefore, we only need to measure $X\\otimes (H-T)$ and $Y\\otimes (H-T)$.\n"
"The contribution from $T$ is reconstructed classically using the already measured overlap matrix element $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"es el elemento de matriz del Hamiltoniano desplazado.\n"
"Por lo tanto, solo necesitamos medir $X\\otimes (H-T)$ y $Y\\otimes (H-T)$.\n"
"La contribución de $T$ se reconstruye clásicamente utilizando el elemento de matriz de solapamiento ya medido $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this example, a natural choice is the diagonal part of the Heisenberg Hamiltonian,\n"
msgstr "En este ejemplo, una elección natural es la parte diagonal del Hamiltoniano de Heisenberg,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2} Z_iZ_{i+1}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2} Z_iZ_{i+1}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because the reference state is a computational-basis state, it is an eigenstate of every $Z_iZ_{i+1}$ term.\n"
msgstr "Dado que el estado de referencia es un estado de la base computacional, es un autoestado de cada término $Z_iZ_{i+1}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "However, a more advantageous choice is to include not only the diagonal $ZZ$ terms, but also the $XX+YY$ terms that annihilate the reference state.\n"
msgstr "Sin embargo, una elección más ventajosa es incluir no solo los términos diagonales $ZZ$, sino también los términos $XX+YY$ que anulan el estado de referencia.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each neighboring pair, the operator $XX+YY$ satisfies\n"
msgstr "Para cada par de vecinos, el operador $XX+YY$ satisface\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"(XX+YY)|00\\rangle = 0,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"(XX+YY)|11\\rangle = 0,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"(XX+YY)|00\\rangle = 0,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"(XX+YY)|11\\rangle = 0,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and\n"
msgstr "and\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"(XX+YY)|01\\rangle = 2|10\\rangle,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"(XX+YY)|10\\rangle = 2|01\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"(XX+YY)|01\\rangle = 2|10\\rangle,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"(XX+YY)|10\\rangle = 2|01\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Therefore, the $XX+YY$ term contributes only when the two neighboring qubits have different occupations in the reference bitstring.\n"
"If the two qubits are both $0$ or both $1$, the term annihilates the reference state and can also be shifted out.\n"
msgstr ""
"Por lo tanto, el término $XX+YY$ contribuye solo cuando los dos Qubits vecinos tienen ocupaciones diferentes en la cadena de bits de referencia.\n"
"Si ambos Qubits son $0$ o ambos son $1$, el término anula el estado de referencia y también puede desplazarse.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let $|\\psi_{\\rm ref}\\rangle = |z_0\\cdots z_{n-1}\\rangle$, where $z_i \\in \\{0,1\\}$.\n"
"Thus, we can choose\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T=\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2} Z_iZ_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"\\sum_{z_i={z_{i+1}}}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"X_iX_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"Y_iY_{i+1}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sea $|\\psi_{\\rm ref}\\rangle = |z_0\\cdots z_{n-1}\\rangle$, donde $z_i \\in \\{0,1\\}$.\n"
"Así, podemos elegir\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T=\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2} Z_iZ_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"\\sum_{z_i={z_{i+1}}}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"X_iX_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"Y_iY_{i+1}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This operator still satisfies\n"
msgstr "Este operador todavía satisface\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T|\\psi_0\\rangle = \\tau |\\psi_0\\rangle ,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T|\\psi_0\\rangle = \\tau |\\psi_0\\rangle ,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"because the $ZZ$ terms act diagonally on $|\\psi_0\\rangle$, while the shifted $XX+YY$ terms give zero.\n"
"The corresponding eigenvalue is therefore determined only by the $ZZ$ terms,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\tau = \\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\n"
"(-1)^{z_i}\n"
"(-1)^{z_{i+1}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"porque los términos $ZZ$ actúan diagonalmente sobre $|\\psi_0\\rangle$, mientras que los términos desplazados $XX+YY$ dan cero.\n"
"El autovalor correspondiente está por lo tanto determinado únicamente por los términos $ZZ$,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\tau = \\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\n"
"(-1)^{z_i}\n"
"(-1)^{z_{i+1}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With this choice, the shifted Hamiltonian becomes:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H-T = \\sum_{z_i\\ne z_{i+1}}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"X_iX_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"Y_iY_{i+1}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Con esta elección, el Hamiltoniano desplazado se convierte en:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H-T = \\sum_{z_i\\ne z_{i+1}}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"X_iX_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"Y_iY_{i+1}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As a result, only the edges with different occupations in the reference state need to be measured.\n"
"All $ZZ$ terms and all inactive $XX+YY$ terms are reconstructed through the overlap contribution $\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}$, or give zero contribution by construction.\n"
msgstr ""
"Como resultado, solo es necesario medir los bordes con ocupaciones diferentes en el estado de referencia.\n"
"Todos los términos $ZZ$ y todos los términos $XX+YY$ inactivos se reconstruyen a través de la contribución de solapamiento $\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}$, o dan una contribución cero por construcción.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This gives a smaller observable than shifting only the diagonal part.\n"
"In particular, for a computational-basis reference state with a localized excitation, only the edges adjacent to the excitation remain in $H-T$.\n"
"Therefore, the number of Pauli terms in $X\\otimes(H-T)$ and $Y\\otimes(H-T)$ can be substantially reduced, while the reconstructed matrix element\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Esto da un observable más pequeño que desplazar solo la parte diagonal.\n"
"En particular, para un estado de referencia de la base computacional con una excitación localizada, solo los bordes adyacentes a la excitación permanecen en $H-T$.\n"
"Por lo tanto, el número de términos de Pauli en $X\\otimes(H-T)$ y $Y\\otimes(H-T)$ puede reducirse sustancialmente, mientras que el elemento de matriz reconstruido\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "remains exactly the same.\n"
msgstr "permanece exactamente igual.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Paso 2: Optimizar el problema para la ejecución en hardware cuántico {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we turn the abstract extended-swap-test circuit into a hardware-oriented template.\n"
"Before that, we further optimize the circuit in the abstract level first.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ahora convertimos el circuito abstracto de prueba de intercambio extendida en una plantilla orientada al hardware.\n"
"Antes de eso, optimizamos aún más el circuito primero a nivel abstracto.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare Hamiltonian term ordering {#compare-hamiltonian-term-ordering}"
msgstr "Comparar el ordenamiento de términos del Hamiltoniano {#compare-hamiltonian-term-ordering}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, we compare different orderings of the Pauli terms in the Heisenberg Hamiltonian for the Hamiltonian simulation.\n"
"The Hamiltonian itself is unchanged, but the ordering affects how the product-formula circuit is generated and how much the structure can be parallelized in the circuit.\n"
"For example, the naive ordering lists all nearest-neighbor $XX$ terms, then all $YY$ terms, then all $ZZ$ terms.\n"
"This places adjacent edges such as $(0,1)$ and $(1,2)$ next to each other, so they cannot be executed in parallel.\n"
"The even-then-odd ordering visits disjoint even edges first, followed by odd edges, which exposes parallel two-qubit layers.\n"
"The even-odd edge-grouped ordering goes one step further: for each edge, it keeps the local $XX$, $YY$, and $ZZ$ terms together, while still visiting even edges before odd edges.\n"
"We expect the even-then-odd and even-odd edge-grouped orderings to reduce circuit depth by exposing parallel two-qubit layers, and the edge-grouped ordering to additionally reduce the Trotter error because the local two-qubit interaction on the same edge is handled as a compact block.\n"
msgstr ""
"Primero, comparamos diferentes ordenamientos de los términos de Pauli en el Hamiltoniano de Heisenberg para la simulación del Hamiltoniano.\n"
"El Hamiltoniano en sí no cambia, pero el ordenamiento afecta cómo se genera el circuito de fórmula de producto y cuánto se puede paralelizar la estructura en el circuito.\n"
"Por ejemplo, el ordenamiento ingenuo enumera todos los términos $XX$ de vecinos más cercanos, luego todos los términos $YY$, luego todos los términos $ZZ$.\n"
"Esto coloca bordes adyacentes como $(0,1)$ y $(1,2)$ uno al lado del otro, por lo que no pueden ejecutarse en paralelo.\n"
"El ordenamiento par-luego-impar visita primero los bordes pares disjuntos, seguidos de los bordes impares, lo que expone capas paralelas de dos Qubits.\n"
"El ordenamiento agrupado por bordes par-impar va un paso más allá: para cada borde, mantiene juntos los términos locales $XX$, $YY$ y $ZZ$, mientras sigue visitando los bordes pares antes que los impares.\n"
"Esperamos que los ordenamientos par-luego-impar y agrupado por bordes par-impar reduzcan la profundidad del circuito al exponer capas paralelas de dos Qubits, y que el ordenamiento agrupado por bordes reduzca adicionalmente el error de Trotter porque la interacción local de dos Qubits en el mismo borde se maneja como un bloque compacto.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Pauli evolutions with different term ordering](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/ham_ordering.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Pauli evolutions with different term ordering](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/ham_ordering.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Hamiltonian ordering also affects the Trotter error.\n"
"If we place noncommuting terms next to each other, the basis transitions occur more often, which induces more Trotter error.\n"
"By grouping terms that require the same Pauli-basis transformation, redundant basis-changes can be avoided.\n"
msgstr ""
"El ordenamiento del Hamiltoniano también afecta al error de Trotter.\n"
"Si colocamos términos que no conmutan uno al lado del otro, las transiciones de base ocurren con más frecuencia, lo que induce más error de Trotter.\n"
"Al agrupar términos que requieren la misma transformación de base de Pauli, se pueden evitar cambios de base redundantes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, the comparison uses the largest evolution time that appears in the first-row Krylov estimates,\n"
"$t_{\\max} = (r-1)\\Delta t,$\n"
"using the same transpilation condition.\n"
msgstr ""
"Aquí, la comparación utiliza el tiempo de evolución más grande que aparece en las estimaciones de Krylov de la primera fila,\n"
"$t_{\\max} = (r-1)\\Delta t,$\n"
"utilizando la misma condición de transpilación.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In order to measure the Trotter error, we use **process infidelity** between the Trotterized circuit and the exact Hamiltonian evolution,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\text{Infidelity}(U,V)\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Para medir el error de Trotter, utilizamos la **infidelidad de proceso** entre el circuito trotterizado y la evolución exacta del Hamiltoniano,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\text{Infidelity}(U,V)\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1-F(U,V)\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"1-F(U,V)\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1 - \\frac{|\\operatorname{Tr}(U^\\dagger V)|^2}{d^2},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"where $d=2^n$ is the dimension of the Hilbert space.\n"
msgstr ""
"1 - \\frac{|\\operatorname{Tr}(U^\\dagger V)|^2}{d^2},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"where $d=2^n$ is the dimension of the Hilbert space.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This diagnostic uses dense matrices, so it is suitable for this small 12-qubit example but not intended as a scalable subroutine.\n"
msgstr "Este diagnóstico utiliza matrices densas, por lo que es adecuado para este pequeño ejemplo de 12 Qubits, pero no está diseñado como una subrutina escalable.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We first keep the synthesis rule fixed to one first-order Trotter step and vary only the Pauli-term ordering.\n"
"The goal of this comparison is mainly to see how much circuit depth and two-qubit cost can be reduced by exposing disjoint nearest-neighbor edges to the transpiler.\n"
msgstr ""
"Primero mantenemos fija la regla de síntesis en un paso de Trotter de primer orden y solo variamos el ordenamiento de términos de Pauli.\n"
"El objetivo de esta comparación es principalmente ver cuánto se puede reducir la profundidad del circuito y el coste de dos Qubits al exponer bordes de vecinos más cercanos disjuntos al transpilador.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-1.avif)\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-3.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-3.avif)\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-5.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-5.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At `reps=1`, we observe that even-then-odd and even-odd edge-grouped orderings both collapse the depth from 15 to 6 by exposing parallel two-qubit layers, while the two-qubit gate count stays the same across all three orderings.\n"
"However, all three orderings have infidelity close to 1, so we sweep the number of Trotter repetitions to separate the orderings more clearly.\n"
"As the number of repetitions grows, the infidelity of `even-odd edge-grouped` ordering drops faster than the other two, reaching 0.045 at `reps=8` versus 0.075 for naive and even-then-odd ordering.\n"
msgstr ""
"Con `reps=1`, observamos que los ordenamientos par-luego-impar y agrupado por bordes par-impar colapsan la profundidad de 15 a 6 al exponer capas paralelas de dos Qubits, mientras que el número de puertas de dos Qubits se mantiene igual en los tres ordenamientos.\n"
"Sin embargo, los tres ordenamientos tienen una infidelidad cercana a 1, por lo que barremos el número de repeticiones de Trotter para separar los ordenamientos con mayor claridad.\n"
"A medida que aumenta el número de repeticiones, la infidelidad del ordenamiento `even-odd edge-grouped` cae más rápido que las otras dos, alcanzando 0.045 en `reps=8` frente a 0.075 para el ordenamiento ingenuo y par-luego-impar.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare product-formula synthesis {#compare-product-formula-synthesis}"
msgstr "Comparar la síntesis de fórmula de producto {#compare-product-formula-synthesis}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we explore different advanced settings of Trotterization, with the fixed Hamiltonian ordering to the even-odd edge-grouped ordering.\n"
"We consider first-order Lie-Trotter, second-order Suzuki-Trotter, and fourth-order Suzuki-Trotter.\n"
msgstr ""
"A continuación, exploramos diferentes configuraciones avanzadas de Trotterización, con el ordenamiento del Hamiltoniano fijado al ordenamiento agrupado por bordes par-impar.\n"
"Consideramos Lie-Trotter de primer orden, Suzuki-Trotter de segundo orden y Suzuki-Trotter de cuarto orden.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Lie-Trotter gives the shallowest circuit but has the largest error, while the fourth-order Suzuki-Trotter is more accurate but increases the circuit depth.\n"
"For the rest of the tutorial, we choose second-order Suzuki-Trotter because it gives a small-depth circuit while substantially reducing the Trotter error relative to the first-order formula.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lie-Trotter da el circuito menos profundo pero tiene el mayor error, mientras que el Suzuki-Trotter de cuarto orden es más preciso pero aumenta la profundidad del circuito.\n"
"Para el resto del tutorial, elegimos Suzuki-Trotter de segundo orden porque proporciona un circuito de poca profundidad mientras reduce sustancialmente el error de Trotter en relación con la fórmula de primer orden.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remove the controlled time-evolution gate {#remove-the-controlled-time-evolution-gate}"
msgstr "Eliminar la puerta de evolución temporal controlada {#remove-the-controlled-time-evolution-gate}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the extended swap test, controlling time evolution with a single ancilla qubit requires the ancilla to control many gates across the system.\n"
"This can introduce substantial routing overhead and, in the worst case, effectively requires all-to-one connectivity.\n"
"To avoid this, further optimization is possible by replacing the controlled time-evolution gate with a control-free version, exploiting the symmetry of the Hamiltonian.\n"
"Let's observe the following circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"En la prueba de intercambio extendida, controlar la evolución temporal con un único Qubit ancilla requiere que el ancilla controle muchas puertas a través del sistema.\n"
"Esto puede introducir una sobrecarga de enrutamiento sustancial y, en el peor de los casos, requerir efectivamente conectividad de todos-a-uno.\n"
"Para evitar esto, es posible una optimización adicional al reemplazar la puerta de evolución temporal controlada por una versión sin control, aprovechando la simetría del Hamiltoniano.\n"
"Observemos el siguiente circuito.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![circuit optimization](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/circuit_opt.avif)\n"
msgstr "![circuit optimization](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/circuit_opt.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, $B_{\\rm ref}$ prepares the reference state, $B_{\\rm ref}|0^n\\rangle = |\\psi_{0}\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Aquí, $B_{\\rm ref}$ prepara el estado de referencia, $B_{\\rm ref}|0^n\\rangle = |\\psi_{0}\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instead of first preparing $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)|\\psi_0\\rangle$ and then applying $U(t)$ only on the $|1\\rangle$ branch, the circuit directly prepares the two branches as\n"
msgstr "En lugar de preparar primero $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)|\\psi_0\\rangle$ y luego aplicar $U(t)$ solo en la rama $|1\\rangle$, el circuito prepara directamente las dos ramas como\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\quad \\text{and} \\quad\n"
"|1\\rangle|\\psi_d\\rangle ,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\quad \\text{and} \\quad\n"
"|1\\rangle|\\psi_d\\rangle ,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where\n"
msgstr "where\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\psi_d\\rangle = U(d\\Delta t)|\\psi_0\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\psi_d\\rangle = U(d\\Delta t)|\\psi_0\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit first applies a Hadamard gate to the ancilla and prepares the reference state only on the $|1\\rangle$ branch:\n"
msgstr "El circuito primero aplica una puerta Hadamard al ancilla y prepara el estado de referencia solo en la rama $|1\\rangle$:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle B_{\\rm ref}|0^n\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle B_{\\rm ref}|0^n\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then the uncontrolled time-evolution operator is applied to both branches:\n"
msgstr "Luego se aplica el operador de evolución temporal no controlado a ambas ramas:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle U(t)|0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle U(t)|0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Since the Hamiltonian preserves the excitation number, we can see that $|0^n\\rangle$ is its eigenstate, and thus\n"
"the evolution operator only accumulates a phase under the Hamiltonian:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"U(t)|0^n\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Dado que el Hamiltoniano conserva el número de excitación, podemos ver que $|0^n\\rangle$ es su autoestado, y por lo tanto\n"
"el operador de evolución solo acumula una fase bajo el Hamiltoniano:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"U(t)|0^n\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0^n\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0^n\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Therefore,\n"
msgstr "Therefore,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle U(t)|0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle U(t)|0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, $B_{\\rm ref}$ is applied only on the $|0\\rangle$ branch.\n"
msgstr "A continuación, $B_{\\rm ref}$ se aplica solo en la rama $|0\\rangle$.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At this point, the two branches have an extra relative phase. To remove it, we apply the ancilla phase gate\n"
msgstr "En este punto, las dos ramas tienen una fase relativa adicional. Para eliminarla, aplicamos la puerta de fase del ancilla\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"P(-E_{\\rm vac}t)\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"P(-E_{\\rm vac}t)\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This transforms the state as\n"
msgstr "Esto transforma el estado como\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, up to an irrelevant global phase, we finally prepared\n"
msgstr "Así, salvo una fase global irrelevante, finalmente preparamos\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\frac{\n"
"|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"|1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{\n"
"|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"|1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the next code block, we implement this control-free circuit.\n"
msgstr "En el siguiente bloque de código, implementamos este circuito sin control.\n"

